{"id":80408840298909,"type":"album","name":"Introspective","artist":"Pet Shop Boys","year":1988,"weight":26,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/7159-introspective-1.jpg","aoty":75,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"AQnkxlK-kLU","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/pet-shop-boys/introspective-6/","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/7159-pet-shop-boys-introspective.php"},"desc":"Introspective is the fourth album, the third of entirely new music, by the UK electronic music group Pet Shop Boys. It was first released on October 11, 1988 and is the Pet Shop Boys' best-selling album, selling over 4.5 million copies worldwide. It is so named because \"all the songs, although it's a dance album, are introspective\". Perhaps the biggest changes in Pet Shop Boys' sound evident on this album are an increasing attention to orchestration using real orchestras, particularly so on the Trevor Horn-produced \"Left to my own devices,\" which took months to produce. The album was also unusual ."},"artist_ref":{"id":140832654458126,"name":"Pet Shop Boys","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pet_Shop_Boys_live_i_Tivoli.JPG?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":269705969260495,"type":"genre","name":"Disco","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":725,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":223122507869858,"type":"genre","name":"Dance-Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":311,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":57638771788875,"type":"genre","name":"Synthpop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":260,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":65067151178508,"type":"genre","name":"Electronic Dance Music","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":244,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":269779479840283,"type":"genre","name":"Electro-Disco","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":209,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":8421460613911,"type":"genre","name":"Hi-NRG","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":143,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":137759473626080,"name":"RYM Top — Danc